  "body": "## What\nRebases and lands `35da260` (branch `fix/resume-and-dispatch-staleness-gate-umr20260806151638-48cc`,\nalready-open PR #184) onto current `main`. That commit was the real root-cause fix\nauthored under `UMR-20260806-151638-48cc` on 2026-08-06, but it never merged -- PR #184\nhas sat open for 9 days with a stale/conflicting head against `main`.\n\n## Why (RCA context)\nThis PR is the direct deliverable of an RCA task\n(`task-20260815-134035-rca--umr-20260806-083251-604c-killed`, dispatched from\n`compliance-tracker`) investigating why `UMR-20260806-083251-604c` (`status=killed`)\nwas blindly re-dispatched about 7h after being correctly flagged `STALE-QUEUED`.\n\nRoot cause (confirmed via the killed row's own `reason` field plus independently\nre-verified against `resource_governor.py`/`dispatch-tick.py` source):\n`flag_stale_queued_tasks()` correctly flagged 4 real rows (this one among them) as\nstale, but `next_queued_task()` never checked that flag before selecting a row to\ndispatch -- detection existed, enforcement did not. `35da260` closes exactly that gap\n(plus adds matching defense-in-depth staleness gating to `dispatch-tick.py`'s\n`resume_interrupted_workers_tick()`).\n\nThis gap was still live on current `main` as of this PR -- `next_queued_task()` on\n`main` had no age check at all; verified directly by diffing the function against\n`35da260` before starting this rebase.\n\n## What changed in this rebase vs. the original commit\n- `resource_governor.py`: applied cleanly, no conflicts.\n- `dispatch-tick.py`: one real conflict in `resume_interrupted_workers_tick()` --\n  `main` had independently grown a `skipped_dead`/`_is_permanently_dead_resume()`\n  check (UMR-20260813-235702, landed after 35da260 was originally authored) that\n  35da260's branch never saw. Resolved by keeping both: the function now returns\n  `resumed`/`skipped_running`/`skipped_duplicate`/`skipped_dead`/`flagged_stale`,\n  all five independent gates intact.\n- `tests/test_ocid_evidence_supersession.py`: original commit's fix (dynamic\n  `ts_submitted` relative to `now`, replacing a hardcoded 2026-08-04 literal that the\n  new staleness gate would otherwise falsely trip) applied cleanly.\n\n## Verification\n- `python3 -m pytest tests/test_resume_stale_task_flagged_not_replayed.py\n  tests/test_flag_stale_queued_tasks.py tests/test_resume_interrupted_workers_bounded_retry.py\n  tests/test_resume_interrupted_workers_no_duplicate_row.py tests/test_umr_reuse_on_resume.py\n  tests/test_ocid_evidence_supersession.py -q` -> **27 passed**.\n- Broader sweep: `pytest tests/ -k \"dispatch_tick or resource_governor or queue or resume or stale or next_queued\"`\n  -> **120 passed, 1 failed**. The 1 failure\n  (`test_stop_work_order_gate.py::test_dispatch_one_defense_in_depth_blocks_preexisting_queued_row`)\n  is a pre-existing environmental flake unrelated to this diff: it asserts\n  `blocked_stop_work_order` but got `deferred`/`cap_exhausted` (`running_worker_count: 5,\n  cap: 5`) -- real live concurrent workers on this shared host consumed the dispatch\n  cap before the stop-work-order gate was reached. This diff touches neither\n  `dispatch_one()` nor the stop-work-order gate.\n\n## Disposition of #184\nSupersedes #184 (same commit, same author intent, just rebased past 9 days of\nconflicting `main` history plus the `skipped_dead` merge). Closing #184 as superseded\nby this PR.\n\nGoverning UMR: `UMR-20260806-071025-1d28`. Original fix UMR: `UMR-20260806-151638-48cc`.\nThis RCA task's UMR: `UMR-20260806-083251-604c`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n",
